    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2YWjtKsLbFBfV3ynQseWxLE)_\n\n## What\nIn `sp-posframe` (and its literate doc):\n- The `vertico-posframe-border` face takes the background of the posframe, so the 4 pixel border (`vertico-posframe-border-width`) reads as padding. It is re-applied on `enable-theme-functions`, so it follows theme changes.\n- New `sp-posframe-dim-always` (default `t`): every posframe prompt dims the frame behind it, removed on exit by the existing undim hook. Set to `nil` to keep the old per-command lists.\n- CHANGELOG entry under Open pull requests.\n\n## Not tested\nNothing was run in Emacs: the container has none, so no GUI or batch check. Please try `M-x`, `find-file` and a theme switch. If the border colour does not update until the next prompt, tell me.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9cVX4xhp367pqb88n)_",
